Provenance
----------
All source code in this repository was written for Auralynx. No source files were copied from
other projects. Knowledge of the Apple Accessory Protocol (AAP) and of Apple Continuity / Proximity
Pairing advertisement formats was obtained from public documentation and source code published by
the projects listed below (all GPL-3.0). Protocol facts (byte layouts, constants) are not
expressive works, but these projects are credited because Auralynx would not exist without their
reverse-engineering effort:

  - LibrePods (https://github.com/kavishdevar/librepods), GPL-3.0, Kavish Devar and contributors:
    "AAP Definitions", opcode and control-command documentation, per-model capability table.
  - CAPod (https://github.com/d4rken-org/capod), GPL-3.0, Matthias Urhahn (d4rken) and contributors:
    proximity pairing payload layout, model codes, key-exchange and encrypted battery layout.
  - OpenPods (https://github.com/adolfintel/OpenPods), GPL-3.0, Federico Dossena: early BLE status research.
  - apple-wireshark (https://github.com/pabloaul/apple-wireshark): AAP/Continuity dissector.

Academic sources: Martin et al., "Handoff All Your Privacy", PoPETs 2019; Celosia and Cunche,
"Discontinued Privacy", PoPETs 2020; Brown and Duda, "A Structural Model for Binaural Sound
Synthesis", IEEE TSAP 1998; R. Bristow-Johnson, "Cookbook formulae for audio EQ biquad filter
coefficients"; Bluetooth Core Specification v5.x, Vol 3 Part H (RPA resolution test vectors).

